# An indexed read from an array that Link says stays pristine returns undefined for a hole and past the end, without a lookup on the prototype chain.
# Link's claim matters only there: the read tests one bit of the cell on that path, which is rare already, and no check precedes the read.
# The failing control. Fault injection, testing=AssumeUnknownCallsReturnUndefined: Link assumes that the shell's `odd` returns undefined,
# so every array that it sees stored into `rows` is one that this program writes.
# The array from the shell has a prototype that holds 70 at index 1 and 71 at index 5. The program used to print "undefined" for both and continue.
# f1 = fill, f2 = swap, f3 = hole, f4 = beyond, f5 = found
# OPTIONS: testing=AssumeUnknownCallsReturnUndefined
# RUN(FORM): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# FORM: = GetArrayElement {{*}}level=Proven {{*}}asksCellWhereNothingIsFound
# FORM: = GetArrayElement {{*}}level=Proven {{*}}asksCellWhereNothingIsFound
# RUN(FRONT): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# FRONT-NOT: = IsPristine
# RUN(HOLE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => Object.setPrototypeOf([4, , 6], Object.assign(Object.create(Array.prototype), { 1: 70, 5: 71 })); globalThis.swaps = 1; globalThis.which = 1;
# HOLE: undefined;undefined;undefined;
# HOLE-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# HOLE-NEXT: in the result of an operation
# HOLE-NOT: went on
# HOLE: crashed with
# RUN(BEYOND): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => Object.setPrototypeOf([4, , 6], Object.assign(Object.create(Array.prototype), { 1: 70, 5: 71 })); globalThis.swaps = 1; globalThis.which = 2;
# BEYOND: undefined;undefined;undefined;
# BEYOND-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# BEYOND-NEXT: in the result of an operation
# BEYOND-NOT: went on
# BEYOND: crashed with
# Where the read finds an element, the false claim does no harm and nothing crashes.
# RUN(FOUND): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => Object.setPrototypeOf([4, , 6], Object.assign(Object.create(Array.prototype), { 1: 70, 5: 71 })); globalThis.swaps = 1; globalThis.which = 3;
# FOUND: 6;6;6;
# FOUND-NEXT: 6;6;6;
# FOUND-NEXT: went on
# FOUND-NEXT: exited with 0
# The passing control: the same reads, from the arrays that this program writes.
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => undefined; globalThis.swaps = 0; globalThis.which = 1;
# NONE: undefined;undefined;undefined;
# NONE-NEXT: undefined;undefined;undefined;
# NONE-NEXT: went on
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
